# Build context exclusions.
#
# Docker's build context and git tracking are INDEPENDENT. `.gitignore` keeps a file out
# of the repository; this file keeps it out of the image. A file can be in one, both, or
# neither — and `backend/data/city.mmdb` is deliberately gitignored but NOT dockerignored,
# so it ships in the image while never reaching GitHub.
#
# Everything below is excluded because it is either regenerable, machine-specific, or
# large enough to slow every build for no runtime benefit.

# Python bytecode and caches — regenerated on import, and a stale .pyc for a deleted
# module can shadow the deletion.
#
# **`**/` is required.** A bare `__pycache__/` matches only at the CONTEXT ROOT, not in
# subdirectories — dockerignore uses Go's filepath.Match semantics, not gitignore's. Measured
# before this fix: the image carried 346 .pyc files from cpython-311, -312 and -314 (the host
# venv and the system python) while the image itself runs 3.10. Inert, because Python rejects a
# mismatched magic number — but stale bytecode from three foreign interpreters was being shipped
# to production, and the pattern that was supposed to prevent it read as though it did.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# Local virtualenvs. Never useful in an image, and often gigabytes.
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/env/

# Secrets. `.env` must NOT be baked in — compose injects it at runtime, so an image
# carrying one would leak credentials to anyone who pulls it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tests and notebooks. Excluded to keep the runtime image lean; CI runs them from the
# source tree, not from the image.
#
# Consequence worth knowing: `docker compose exec api pytest` collects NOTHING, because the
# image has no tests. Run them with the repo mounted instead —
#   docker compose run --rm -v "$(pwd):/repo:ro" -w /repo/backend api python -m pytest
# ...or locally after `make venv`.
tests/
notebooks/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT excluded, and deliberately so
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   data/city.mmdb        The IP -> city database. Gitignored (124MB, and DB-IP's
#                         licence is CC-BY rather than something we can redistribute
#                         in a public repo) but baked into the image so a deployed
#                         container resolves cities with no runtime download and no
#                         third-party call. Present only on machines that ran
#                         `make geoip` — the build simply omits it elsewhere, and
#                         `iam/geo.py` degrades to showing raw IPs.
#
#   app/ml/weights/*.pt   Same pattern: gitignored, shipped when present, and
#                         inference falls back to documented physical thresholds
#                         when absent.
